	<string name="help_text">
# Start

Open Playlists. Add an Xtream login, an M3U URL, an M3U file, or a Stalker portal (address and MAC). Xtream and Stalker bring their own guide. For M3U, add its guide URL.

# Main screen

Search is at the top. It searches every group in the section. Voice, next to it, fills it by speech. Back clears it.

Below: Live TV, Movies, Series. Then Playlists, On now, Guide search, Recordings, More.

Groups are on the left, the list on the right. Both have headings. Picking a group moves you to the list.

# Items

Activate to play. A series opens its episodes.

Actions menu: play in another app, favourite, details, guide, record, download. Without TalkBack: long-press, or the Menu key.

# Guide

On now lists everything airing. A channel\'s guide plays past programmes marked catch-up, and schedules future ones. Guide search finds upcoming programmes.

# Player

Buttons: Pause, Audio, Record, Cast, Full screen, Close. Keys: play/pause, A for audio, F for full screen.

Full screen hides the buttons. Tap, Back, OK or F brings them back.

Audio description is picked when a channel has it. A track you pick is remembered per channel.

# Updates

The app checks for a new version once a day. More, Check for updates checks now. Android asks you to confirm every install.

# Recordings

Saved to Movies/AccessibleIPTV. Scheduled recordings start a minute early and survive a restart.
	</string>
